{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://openworkplacehealth.org/schemas/v0.2/AbsenceEpisode.json",
  "title": "OWHS AbsenceEpisode v0.2",
  "description": "Reported sickness-absence episode with versioned reason-category mapping. No direct identifiers.",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "episodeId": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
    },
    "pseudonymId": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^owhs:pseudo:[0-9a-f]{16,64}$",
      "description": "Per-org opaque pseudonym; never a direct identifier"
    },
    "reasonCode": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "minor-illness",
        "musculoskeletal",
        "other",
        "mental-health",
        "gastrointestinal",
        "respiratory",
        "eye-ear-nose-mouth-dental",
        "genito-urinary",
        "heart-blood-pressure-circulation",
        "headaches-migraines",
        "prefers-not-to-give-details"
      ],
      "$comment": "codelist:absence-reason@0.2.0. Reported reason categories following the ONS 2025 workbook plus its separate non-disclosure response; not diagnoses. The crosswalk from the v0.1 six-code list is codelists/mappings/absence-reason-ons-2025-v1.json; a legacy other is not upgraded automatically."
    },
    "startDate": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date"
    },
    "endDate": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date"
    },
    "workingDaysLost": {
      "type": "number",
      "minimum": 0,
      "$comment": "ONS 7.5-hour working-day unit"
    },
    "workingHoursLost": {
      "type": "number",
      "minimum": 0
    },
    "fitNoteFlag": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "workRelatedFlag": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "clinicalCauseCode": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[0-9]{6,18}$",
      "$comment": "OPTIONAL SNOMED CT; affiliate-licence caveat; never conformance-required"
    },
    "sourceProvenance": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "sourceType"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "sourceType": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "hris",
            "manual",
            "broker",
            "oh-provider"
          ],
          "$comment": "codelist:source-type@0.1.0 — OWHS record provenance"
        },
        "sourceProvider": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "sourceId": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    },
    "ext": {
      "type": "object",
      "$comment": "Extension namespaces and values are structurally checked. The named identifier keys are prohibited recursively; OHEpisode also prohibits its named clinical-content keys recursively. This is not detection of identifiers or clinical meaning hidden in allowed keys or values. All extensions remain subject to P1-P5 and their applicable profile. A core-only pass does not establish profile or Level 3 conformance.",
      "propertyNames": {
        "pattern": "^owhs-[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$",
        "maxLength": 64
      },
      "additionalProperties": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/owhsExtensionObject"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "episodeId",
    "pseudonymId",
    "reasonCode",
    "startDate",
    "sourceProvenance"
  ],
  "allOf": [
    {
      "$comment": "P1 (no direct identifiers) is enforced structurally by \"additionalProperties\": false on this object and on every nested object, which rejects any property not declared here, including name, nino, email, dateOfBirth and address. A key-based rule cannot reach an identifier written into the value of a permitted string field; that part of P1 is a producer obligation, stated in the privacy profile. The previous allOf member duplicated additionalProperties and claimed to forbid identifiers \"anywhere\", which was not true of values."
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Chronology (endDate not before startDate) is not expressible in JSON Schema, which compares an instance against a schema and never one field against another. It is the named Level 1 cross-field rule C1, listed in the specification and implemented in tools/validate.py. The previous allOf member re-asserted the type and format of endDate and enforced no ordering."
    }
  ],
  "$defs": {
    "owhsExtensionObject": {
      "type": "object",
      "propertyNames": {
        "not": {
          "enum": [
            "name",
            "nino",
            "email",
            "dateOfBirth",
            "address"
          ]
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/owhsExtensionValue"
      }
    },
    "owhsExtensionValue": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "number",
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/owhsExtensionValue"
          }
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/owhsExtensionObject"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

